    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Total consignment CFT volume</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Cubic feet (CFT) measure the three‑dimensional space your items occupy. For local moves, packers often apply a flat rate per CFT, while intercity rates scale with volume because larger loads fill more of the carrier’s capacity, influencing the “movers and packers cost one city to another.” A higher CFT usually pushes the price up, but ISO‑certified packers and movers may offer volume‑based discounts.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Transit kilometers</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The distance between the origin and destination is the most obvious cost driver. Local shifts (within Deoghar) are billed per kilometer or per hour, whereas intercity trips add a per‑kilometer surcharge that reflects road wear, driver wages, and time spent in transit.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding-top: 10px;">
